From: ShareOS <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: no 413 after the last part of a request body

uh_client_read_cb() answered 413 Request Entity Too Large when a read
callback returned false with a full buffer in any state but DATA. The
check used the length from before the callback: when the last part of a
POST body arrives as exactly one full buffer, client_data_cb() forwards
it, finishes the request (state DONE) and returns false, and the
finished upload is answered with 413. Over TLS this happens on nearly
every larger upload (16 KB records, 4 KB buffer).

Only answer 413 while the request line or headers are still being read
and the buffer is still full after the callback.

--- a/client.c	2026-10-20 20:11:53.178315408 +0200
+++ b/client.c	2026-10-20 20:11:53.206432206 +0200
@@ -531,8 +531,17 @@
 			break;
 
 		if (!read_cbs[cl->state](cl, str, len)) {
-			if (len == us->r.buffer_len &&
-			    cl->state != CLIENT_STATE_DATA)
+			/*
+			 * Only a request line or header that fills the whole
+			 * buffer is too large. The callback may have consumed
+			 * the buffer and finished the request (the last part of
+			 * an upload arriving as one full buffer, common with
+			 * TLS), so look at the state and buffer after it.
+			 */
+			if ((cl->state == CLIENT_STATE_INIT ||
+			     cl->state == CLIENT_STATE_HEADER) &&
+			    ustream_get_read_buf(us, &len) &&
+			    len == us->r.buffer_len)
 				uh_header_error(cl, 413, "Request Entity Too Large");
 			break;
 		}
